=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might also do something along the lines of Poison Ivy, too. Poisonous touch. Immune to toxins. Reskin a few Atavisms as plant-related powers. Her Nightmare might be some kind of dryad gone very wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or very right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:51:19-08:00","id":789934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/787409-plant-monsters?p=789871#post789871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're going to live in my mind, pay rent! Hunger for Punishment, most likely.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Could very easily be Hunger for Ruin as well. Civilization and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T23:11:58-08:00","id":790115,"title":"","content":"Man, nobody's mentioned The Happening's killer grass yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T07:42:06-08:00","id":790270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/787409-plant-monsters?p=790115#post790115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, nobody's mentioned The Happening's killer grass yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've Tried not too.... That wasn't well done but it does feed into the discussion I guess. Also it's not really a &quot;Monster&quot; The closest i can think of to link it too.. Is <a href=\"http://dc.wikia.com/wiki/The_Green\" target=\"_blank\">The Green</a> from DC Comics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T12:13:53-08:00","id":791733,"title":"","content":"The though springs to mind of a story I remember (I can't remember where from) about a woman who from the front was ethereally beautiful, but from the back she was just a hollow piece of bark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T09:41:43-08:00","id":792758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/787409-plant-monsters?p=791733#post791733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The though springs to mind of a story I remember (I can't remember where from) about a woman who from the front was ethereally beautiful, but from the back she was just a hollow piece of bark.</div> </div> </div> </div>You speak of a nordic folk creature.. I believe its called a huldra.<br /> <br /> here's a Link.. erm.. may be NSFW for tasteful nudity. <a href=\"http://humoncomics.com/huldra-and-troll\" target=\"_blank\">http://humoncomics.com/huldra-and-troll</a><br /> <br /> there are more comics about such creatures at that site.. but it may take a little digging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T12:35:19-08:00","id":817062,"title":"","content":"Forgive me for posting on something from a while back.<br /> \u200bLotus Trees, vampire vines, The Sagebrush Kid, and arguably one of the myths that Slender Man is associated with (ancient sacrifices on the spikes of ceiba trees) are all examples of cryptid/horror plants. There are myths the world over of plants that induce a torpor in those who eat their fruit, then transfigure their sleeping consumers into more trees of what is usually an oddly uniform grove. Plenty of books and extant RPG sources too (plant creature subtype in D&amp;D).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:13:52-08:00","id":817093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/787409-plant-monsters?p=817062#post817062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me for posting on something from a while back.<br /> \u200bLotus Trees, vampire vines, The Sagebrush Kid, and arguably one of the myths that Slender Man is associated with (ancient sacrifices on the spikes of ceiba trees) are all examples of cryptid/horror plants. There are myths the world over of plants that induce a torpor in those who eat their fruit, then transfigure their sleeping consumers into more trees of what is usually an oddly uniform grove. Plenty of books and extant RPG sources too (plant creature subtype in D&amp;D).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A fantastically creepy version of the the 'trees turn you into more of them' would be the Ausren Woods from Numenera","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:17:19-08:00","id":817158,"title":"","content":"Ceiba sacrifices. That one is new to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:33:11-08:00","id":817180,"title":"","content":"If anyone's read A Monster Calls, the Walker/the Green Man could definitely qualify as a plant monster. Especially in the scene where the old ash tree twists into the shape of the monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:13:49-08:00","id":817815,"title":"","content":"I've got a Homebrew Atavism that was designed to work for plant monsters. I'm not sure about the Family. Any suggestions would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Witchwood</b><br /> <br /> When one thinks of monsters, plants do not immediately come to mind. Plants are sedentary, slow things. They cannot chase you, nor can they tear your flesh with claws and teeth, nor can they set your city aflame. All that plants can do is wait and watch and grow, ever so slowly. But that is enough. It is enough for roots to pull down your houses, brick by brick, inch by painful inch. It is enough to <i>know, </i>to know things about the world that humans cannot even dream of. It is enough to outlive generation upon generation of humankind.<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Stamina + Medicine + Lair (purging poisons)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast is a creature of infinite patience and his heart beats in sync with the pulse of the earth itself. He can hear the secret whispers of the trees and ask them to divulge the secrets of the past.<br /> The Beast can communicate with any plant life he can touch and can ask it questions about the past. How much a plant remembers will depend on its age and size (an ancient oak will remember further back than a patch of algae), but the older and larger it is, the less likely it will remember small events. Also, plants do not communicate with words so much as impressions and feelings and do not possess many of the senses that humans do. As a rough rule of thumb, plants will probably remember light and dark, rainfall or watering, drought and things touching them but not much else.<br /> The Beast may also root himself with an Instant action so long as he is standing, lying or sitting on bare earth. This applies the Immobilised Tilt to him but as long as he remains rooted he need not eat or drink (so long as the soil he is rooted on has water and nutrients (e.g. not desert sand)), adds his Lair to dice pools to avoid being moved or knocked over and may roll Stamina + Medicine + Lair to attempt to purge any poisons he is afflicted with and adds Lair to any dice pools to resist the effects of such venoms. De-rooting himself is another Instant action.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As the Beast\u2019s hunger grows, so too does his awareness of and connection with the natural world around him. So long as the Beast can bask in natural sunlight, he heals <u>all</u> Bashing damage every 15 minutes. Additionally, while rooted, the Beast can instinctively sense the position of any kind of plant life in an area equal to (Lair*5 yards) and heals Lethal damage at the rate of 1 point every 6 hours so long as he is constantly exposed to natural sunlight.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With the expenditure of a dot of Satiety, the Beast can channel power into nearby plant life, vastly accelerating its growth. In exchange, the Beast becomes able to shape the growth of any plant that he is bolstering. For each dot of Satiety thus spent, the beast can increase the Size of a plant by his (Lair*5). If the Beast directs the plants to grow into a structure, they deal damage to Structure equal to the Size increased and ignore Durability equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair. The growth takes 30 seconds per point of Size gained.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}